    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57096" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κήλη</span></b> , 
			Att.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλη</span></b>  [prob.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ], ἡ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tumour</i>; esp. <i>rupture,
				hernia</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
			</span></i><i>Aër.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.166
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Lucill.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				11.342
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>hump</i> on a buffalo's back, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				606a16
			</span></i>, in acc. pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλας</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαίτας</span>
			); in human beings, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				276.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.729
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Artem.
				3.45
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλήτης καὶ κάλη Ἀττικοί . . ,
					κηλήτης καὶ κήλη Ἴωνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phryn.
					<u>PS</u>
					p.81
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i> (Cf. ONorse <i>haull</i>, OSlav. <i>kyla</i>, both
				=
			<i>hernia.</i>)</div>
